# PLACEHOLDER — not a real signing key.
#
# Run scripts/init-signing-key.sh on a trusted machine to generate the real
# release signing keypair; it overwrites this file with the public half (which
# you then commit) and writes the private half to a gitignored location.
#
# Until this is replaced with a real ed25519 public key, signature
# verification fails closed: update-image.sh and the deploy scripts refuse to
# import an image they cannot verify against this key. That is intentional —
# set up signing before publishing or deploying a release.
